he gives away any private information - well...

It's quite different on a server like the one you have at MIT. There
you will be typically recorded by user name and user ID as entered in
the password file.

But, even considering Kent's valid critique, the available data set on
NAO is really a/the great source for any analysis, as the OP also said
in his introduction, there's no alternative that I would see anywhere
at the moment.

